  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186172038,
      "id": "b0e7e0a0-9388-5346-ab96-f2dec237c9f5",
      "title": "Sketching the Slope Field of a Differential Equation at Some Isolated Points"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4edeee8e-dc1b-571c-b8d3-e36d9d0409e0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x+(-1)y}{4}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,3)$,$(-1,-1)$,$(-3,-1)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,3)}=\\frac{3(-2)+(-1)(3)}{4}=- \\frac{9}{4}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-1)}=\\frac{3(-1)+(-1)(-1)}{4}=- \\frac{1}{2}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-3,-1)}=\\frac{3(-3)+(-1)(-1)}{4}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](11aaffda7a572e5d68c90142eeb0cbab90849515d58af57ebcd4ef5a9df7e14c.png)",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4ba7cdc6-32fe-5405-a066-945149cf2ba3",
