  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186172038,
      "id": "b0e7e0a0-9388-5346-ab96-f2dec237c9f5",
      "title": "Sketching the Slope Field of a Differential Equation at Some Isolated Points"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a86c1f94-d03b-5ddf-8ca2-4bed720e9e37",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-1-(2)xy?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-1,-1)$,$(-3,3)$,$(-2,0)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-1)}=-1-2(-1)(-1)=-3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-3,3)}=-1-2(-3)(3)=17, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,0)}=-1-2(-2)(0)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](96ea75f963a1ed7abfbab0e95a1435b8a771f1530f6e64712388552f75620aaf.png)",
